External development tools
--------------------------
The optional compiler-built homebrew workflow links original applications with
unmodified devkitPro/libctru at 9b55eda44cf80b971503991e0c78f9bc8fe50425,
https://github.com/devkitPro/libctru, using its zlib-style permission in README.md.
The complete notice is preserved at docs/licenses/libctru.txt. Library source
and devkitARM remain external dependencies; their source/tool binaries are not
included in the source bundle. The optional compiled interactive RPX/WUHB embeds
that original application's ARM executable, including linked libctru and
GCC/newlib support. Keep the libctru notice and existing runtime license texts
with that artifact. The ARM compiler used in this workflow is GCC 15.2.0; the
GCC exception/GPL texts are the same license versions preserved below, not a
claim that it is GCC 16.1.0 or that the ARM and PPC newlib builds are identical.
ARM newlib's complete collected notices are also preserved as
docs/licenses/COPYING.NEWLIB.ARM (devkitPro/newlib devkitPro license-reference
commit 57bd8e1ade3cf46d2e61a72516ac8bfaf8fdfd62).
The linked 3DSX CRT is devkitPro/devkitarm-crtls under MPL 2.0. Its unmodified
3dsx_crt0.s, 3dsx.ld and 3dsx.specs source from commit
1c0c10257c44bbb5a433453bb6bba91582825492 is included at
docs/licenses/devkitarm-crtls/, with the full MPL text at docs/licenses/MPL-2.0.txt.
The rebuilt .crt0 section bytes and relocations match the installed ARM SDK
object; whole-object hashes differ. These sources accompany the covered startup
code in the optional compiled guest. They are not project-authored code or linked
into the native PPC platform as assembly. See the audit receipt at
docs/licenses/devkitarm-crtls/README.md. CTR2WUP's license does not replace their MPL.

The separate CTR2WUP-CIA-Intake Windows x64 utility bundles Microsoft's .NET
10.0.14 runtime and apphost under MIT plus the preserved third-party notices
from the exact restored runtime/host packages. Their LICENSE.TXT and
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.TXT are identical for those packages and accompany the helper
distribution as LICENSE-DOTNET.txt and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES-DOTNET.txt. Copies are
also at docs/licenses/dotnet-runtime-*.txt. This limited console helper is
original intake code, not the final GUI/injector; no SDK, user game or credential
is bundled. Runtime source: https://github.com/dotnet/runtime, v10.0.14.

Encrypted packaging optionally calls the external Python package cryptography
50.0.2, https://github.com/pyca/cryptography. Its Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause
license permits the BSD-3-Clause grant selected here; the full notice is
preserved at docs/licenses/cryptography-LICENSE.BSD. No cryptography, OpenSSL,
CFFI or other native dependency binary is bundled in these source/diagnostic
archives. A future Windows dependency distribution must retain all applicable
package and native dependency notices.

Rust, Cargo, GCC/devkitPPC, newlib, elf2rpl and optional SDK packages remain
external toolchain dependencies. This notice does not assert that their
licenses are identical to WUT's. Redistributing a complete host application or
toolchain bundle requires a dependency-by-dependency notice and source audit.
No ROM, commercial game assets, Nintendo SDK, donor title or credential is
included with this project.

The optional scene encoding tests use external, unmodified nihstro headers at
f4d8659decbfe5d234f04134b5002b82dc515a44 (BSD-3-Clause, copyright 2014 Tony
Wasserka). They are compiled only in a separate reference test, not copied,
linked into the runtime or bundled in distributions. No emulator implementation
is incorporated by the original loader/MOV shader/software scene increment.

